 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are kept in the
+data file as `apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`; `data/seed.json` has one
+development key per role. Roles:
+
+- `viewer`: reads only (`GET`).
+- `cook`: also `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures` and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: everything, including `GET /audit`.
+
+No key or an unknown key answers 401 `unauthorized`; a known key without
+permission answers 403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every non-`GET` request with a known key writes an audit entry
+`{ at, key, method, path, status }` (`key` is the key's name, never the key),
+whatever its status. `GET /audit` lists them newest first, for managers only.
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
